From e5bc329854edc1a86281d6b1440ce7ee1ccbf70e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mouhamed Bassiroou Khouma <Mouhamedbk1002@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 00:03:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(espace-client): full dashboard redesign
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Design direction: ground the UI in the actual product — a printed NFC
business card — rather than a generic SaaS card-grid dashboard.

- client/src/components/client-space/IdCard.tsx: hero component rendering
  the client's fiche as a physical card mockup (navy gradient, chip, plan
  badge, public URL, share/open actions) — reused at smaller scale for
  membership cards in ClientCards
- client/src/components/client-space/FicheOverview.tsx: shared dashboard
  body (hero + échéance status + plan mini-stats + KPI tiles + scan chart +
  latest requests/cards) used by both the single-fiche dashboard route and
  the per-fiche detail route, removing the previous duplication between
  ClientDashboard and FicheClientDetail
- client/src/components/client-space/ScanChart.tsx: recharts area chart
  replacing the manual absolute-positioned <div> bar chart, reused by the
  dashboard and the statistics page
- client/src/components/client-space/KpiTile.tsx, lib/ficheStatus.ts:
  small shared building blocks (KPI tile, échéance/plan/card-status label
  and color helpers)
- client/src/components/ClientLayout.tsx: redesigned shell reusing the
  existing house brand tokens (navy sidebar, amber accent) already
  established by the admin studio and public fiche page; adds a fiche
  switcher for accounts with several fiches, a responsive drawer, and a
  proper user/logout block
- client/src/pages/ClientStats.tsx, ClientRequests.tsx, ClientCards.tsx:
  visual pass to the same design system (panels, status pills, empty
  states)
- client/src/index.css: new client-space token layer (.id-card, .kpi-tile,
  .panel, .status-pill, .activity-row, .client-shell/sidebar/topbar)
  layered onto the existing palette, no new colors introduced
