From cc464a1fa06b1939d858bcdb71ba0887609e1eb5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mouhamed Bassiroou Khouma <Mouhamedbk1002@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 09:00:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix(espace-client): missing /espace-client/connexion
 route + brand the entry screens
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- App.tsx was redirecting logged-out users to /espace-client/connexion,
  a route that did not exist anywhere in the router — they landed on the
  404 page instead of a login screen. Added ClientLogin.tsx and wired it
  in.
- ClientLogin.tsx: branded landing page with a 'Continuer avec Google'
  button, replacing the previous dead end.
- ClientSplash.tsx: shared branded (navy, brand mark, spinner) full-screen
  loading state, replacing the generic bg-slate-950 screens in
  ClientGuard (session check) and InviteConsume (invitation activation) —
  these are literally a new client's first two screens, worth getting
  right.
---
